  "configuration_id": "config_018",
  "reason": "With no prior evidence, the first experiment should establish a strong reference point in the most promising region of the design space. config_018 (multimodal, multiprofile, scgpt, imagenet_vit_l, transformer, weighted) represents the most complete multimodal architecture: it pairs the most advanced RNA encoder (scgpt, a generative pre-trained single-cell model) with the strongest image encoder (ViT-L), uses multiprofile with transformer aggregation to capture multi-view information, and applies weighted fusion. This tests the central hypothesis that a full multimodal pipeline outperforms simpler variants. If it performs well, it sets a high ceiling and I can ablate components in subsequent experiments. If it underperforms, it signals that one or more of the complex components (scgpt, ViT-L, transformer aggregation) may be suboptimal, guiding targeted simplification. As experiment 1 of 10, this maximizes information gain by anchoring the search in the highest-capability region before exploring trade-offs."
}

